--- a/docs/content/manual/manual.yml
+++ b/docs/content/manual/manual.yml
@@ -408,6 +408,14 @@
           only for identifier-like strings).

+          Indexes can be chained with or without an intervening dot:
+          `.foo["bar"]` and `.foo.["bar"]` are equivalent, as are
+          `.foo[0]` and `.foo.[0]`. This also applies to iteration and
+          slicing: `.foo.[]` is equivalent to `.foo[]`, and `.foo.[1:3]`
+          is equivalent to `.foo[1:3]`.
+
+        examples:
+          - program: '.["foo"].["bar"]'
+            input: '{"foo": {"bar": 42}}'
+            output: [42]
+
       - title: "Array Index: `.[<number>]`"
         body: |
PATCH

